 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage 2 — Browser-identity defects
+## Voyage 3 — Browser-identity defects (remaining)
 
 ### State at opening
-- Voyage 1 complete: TodoMVC vanilla JS app implemented, all 31 scenarios pass via happy-dom
-- Cypress acceptance suite (real browser) reports 5 failures due to DOM node detachment
-- Root cause: `render()` in `js/app.js` uses `todoList.innerHTML = ...` which destroys and recreates all `<li>` elements on every state change
-- Additional issue: `.toggle` checkbox not hidden during editing (no CSS rule, no `todomvc-app-css` loaded)
-
-### Acceptance failures (fixed spec, must not change test)
-1. "Mark all as completed" — `cy.eq()` fails: toggle-all re-render destroys all `<li>` references
-2. "Clear complete state of all items" — same: toggle-all re-render
-3. "Mark items as complete" — `cy.find()` fails: single toggle triggers `render()` which rebuilds list
-4. "Un-mark items as complete" — same: single toggle re-render
-5. "Hide other controls when editing" — `.toggle` checkbox is visible during editing, should be hidden
+- Voyage 2 complete: DOM identity fixed (mutate in place, no innerHTML rebuild), toggle hidden during editing via injected CSS
+- 35 scenarios all pass via happy-dom (DOM identity + editing toggle scenarios added)
+- Cypress acceptance suite now reports 2 remaining failures (browser-specific)
+
+### Remaining acceptance failures (fixed spec, must not change test)
+1. "should hide other controls when editing" — `<label>` is visible during editing, should be hidden
+   - Root cause: CSS injection only hides `.toggle`, not the label
+   - New scenario: "Editing hides the label control" — FAILS on current code (pins the missing CSS rule)
+
+2. "should remove the item if an empty text string was entered" — `Failed to execute 'remove' on 'Element': The node to be removed is no longer a child of this node. Perhaps it was moved in a 'blur' event handler?`
+   - Root cause: `render()` → `todoList.innerHTML = ''` removes focused `editInput`, which fires a `blur` event in a real browser. The `blur` handler re-enters `updateTodo()` → `removeTodo()` → `render()`, and the second `render()` tries to `.remove()` an already-detached node.
+   - Not reproducible in happy-dom (blur events don't fire on DOM removal)
+   - PERTURBATION planted at the blur handler seam in `js/app.js:288`
+   - Existing scenarios "Empty edit destroys the todo", "Whitespace-only edit destroys the todo" pin the must-survive behaviour
+   - New scenario "Empty edit via blur destroys the todo" added for explicit blur-path coverage
 
 ### Decisions
-- **DOM identity**: The app must mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place (toggle class/checkbox) instead of rebuilding via `innerHTML`. This preserves browser-held references.
-- **Editing controls**: `.toggle` checkbox must be hidden when the parent `<li>` has `.editing` class (CSS: `.todo-list li.editing .toggle { display: none; }`)
-- 4 new scenarios added to `features/todos.feature` pinning this behaviour
-- `watchbill.json` created with 2 watches: `watch-dom-identity` and `watch-editing-controls`
+- **Label visibility**: CSS rule must also hide the label during editing: `.todo-list li.editing .view label { display: none; }` (or `.todo-list li.editing .view { display: none; }`)
+- **Blur re-entrancy**: The blur handler must guard against re-entrant render calls. The Enter-key handler also calls `li.classList.remove('editing')` on a potentially detached `li` after `updateTodo` removes the item.
+
+### Durable artifacts authored
+- `features/todos.feature`: 2 new scenarios added (editing hides label, empty edit via blur)
+- `js/app.js`: PERTURBATION marker at blur handler (line 288)
+- `watchbill.json`: 2 watches — `watch-editing-controls` and `watch-empty-edit-blur`
 
 ### Next role
-QM → implement step definitions for the 4 new scenarios, then execute watchbill.
-Crew → fix `render()` to mutate in-place; add CSS rule to hide toggle during editing.
+QM → implement step definitions for the new scenarios, execute watchbill, report green.
+Crew → add CSS rule to hide label during editing; fix blur handler re-entrancy.
 Boatswain → custody after QM goes green.
